WEBVTT

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.550
Instant Destruction by Fire!

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.460
Great Kamaitachi!

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:35.090
A snake?

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.940
Be careful. Looks like 
it's a 4,500-year class.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.960
It'll be pretty tough.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:46.110
Hah! What's a measly 4,500 years?

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:48.370
I've been around for sixteen years!

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:51.280
I'm not gonna lose!

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:00.250
Realized you were scared of me, did ya?

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:01.660
Follow it!

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:04.580
Hey!

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:17.170
A Horologue's only instinct is to attack 
humans and eat their time. Why would it run?

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:19.760
You're right. This must mean...

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:23.570
There's someone up ahead 
who controls Horologues.

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:28.650
As far as I could see, there was 
nothing off about the townsfolk.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:33.530
And it doesn't seem like the Horologue 
was summoned by anyone's regret.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:37.450
Which means the problem isn't 
with someone from the town.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:39.300
It's with Couljours itself.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.370
Itself?

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:44.590
Yes. We'll have to inspect 
the entire town again.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:46.790
Let's head back to the entrance.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:56.010
<i>So a Horologue that acts on 
command appears outside town...</i>

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:58.390
<i>A town where time has turned backwards.</i>

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:00.890
<i>There must be a connection.</i>

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:03.640
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:09.480
<i>It's fast!</i>

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:11.340
Leave this to me!

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:21.440
Damn! For its size, that bastard can move!

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.130
And fast, at that.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:24.940
We can barely keep up.

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:28.650
I'm pretty sure it's trying 
to lead us somewhere.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:34.720
Is that why it's running at just 
the right speed for us to keep up,

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:38.630
even though it's fast enough 
to evade our attacks?

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:41.600
Damn! Lead on, then!

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:43.350
We'll chase you down anywhere!

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:45.820
If we can find who's controlling it,

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:49.330
we should be able to figure out why 
time in Couljours is going backwards!

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.020
Investigating is fine.

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:55.870
But we'll work separately. 
There's something I need to do.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:01.800
<i>And we might find a hint on how 
to get Victor's lost time back.</i>

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:07.380
I dunno what's going on,
but this is pretty huge, isn't it?

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:08.860
I'm getting fired up!

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:10.870
If I can take down this bad boy,

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:14.210
I'll be a step closer to being 
the world's top villain!

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.430
Blaze, what's that on your back?

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.840
It keeps flashing in and out 
of sight. It's annoying me.

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:22.540
That brat at the clinic told me,

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:25.720
"I came up with a cool nickname for you."

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.290
And then he gave me this!

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:29.850
* "Chickenshit"

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.850
He said it means "super strong fire dragon"!

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:32.980
That little brat actually gets it!

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:10.450
March 29 8:43

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:24.860
What's the matter, Alexander?

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:27.670
Y-You're... S-Something awful's happened!

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:31.110
Please calm down. What happened?

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:33.600
There's no time for this!

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:37.390
I was making a house call when 
I got a call from a patient.

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:39.860
Since no one was at the clinic to help,

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:44.570
Eve started to spit up blood while 
she was drawing, and now she's...

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:47.990
She's unconscious! I have to 
treat her at once, or she'll...

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:49.630
The past can't be changed!

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:52.530
No matter what you do for them now,
it'll mean nothing!

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:57.590
I'll help you.

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:05.050
Eve!

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:07.470
Oh... Doctor, your wife...

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:14.680
You're late, idiot father!

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:18.160
Thanks to your son's first aid,

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:21.520
your wife seems to have stabilized.

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:24.110
Victor...

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:26.990
Honestly...

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:29.940
I have an important entrance exam today.

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:31.560
Now I'll be late.

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:35.080
All you people do is get in my way.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:38.460
I-I see... Thanks, Victor.

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:40.950
H-Have you had breakfast?

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:43.790
You can't think on an empty stomach, right?

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:46.460
I took care of that ages ago.

00:06:46.730 --> 00:06:48.620
I don't need advice from you.

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:49.840
It's just a waste of time.

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:51.500
R-Right...

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:55.360
You can always handle things on your own.

00:06:58.340 --> 00:06:59.080
Wait!

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:01.320
Something's wrong with Eve!

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:02.270
What?

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:14.280
She's showing signs of cyanosis.

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:17.260
Her blood pressure, her pulse...

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:20.330
No! What do I do?

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:23.110
Alexander, calm down and 
deal with the situation!

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:28.380
What she needs right now 
is a blood transfusion.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:30.390
Then let's do it right away!

00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:31.930
But there's a problem.

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:36.180
Her blood type is AB negative.

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:41.850
Only one in every 2,000 people 
has that blood type.

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:45.340
If the blood we give her doesn't match,

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.860
it'll only accelerate her death.

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:57.830
<i>I didn't oppose you out of hatred.</i>

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:01.080
<i>But this is a false past 
that someone has created.</i>

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:03.070
<i>They may be trying to hurt you</i>

00:08:03.070 --> 00:08:05.440
<i>and prevent you from escaping.</i>

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:09.020
<i>In which case, I can't waste any time!</i>

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:09.170
<b>Speed Up</b>

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:16.490
That was pathetic!

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:19.260
Check out <i>my</i> bad self!

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:19.260
<b>Speed Up</b>

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:28.460
What the hell?!

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:30.610
Blaze!

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:33.610
Dumbass! Go on without me!

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:42.700
That's no good at all.

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:45.830
You were always such a high-maintenance boy.

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:49.090
Why did you pick today of all 
days to not follow Victor?

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:54.480
So there you have it.

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:57.510
I'm going to investigate around town,
even if I have to do it alone.

00:08:58.130 --> 00:08:59.950
You two can do whatever you want.

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:03.340
If there's gonna be a fight, I'm there.

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:04.950
I'm coming, too.

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:07.940
I'm trying to lose weight, 
so I'll take the exercise.

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:10.590
Have it your way.

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:20.410
Of course there's no way it'd be fun 
to hang out with a four-eyes like you.

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:24.150
But what I hate even more is 
the way my darling's acting now.

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:27.420
You might not have noticed,

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:31.920
but since we met his mother, his eyes 
always look sad when he smiles.

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:36.550
I love my darling's bright, cheerful smile.

00:09:37.330 --> 00:09:40.780
When he's happy, I can be happy, too.

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:44.640
But when he's sad, it hurts me, too.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:54.150
That's why I hate this town. 
All it does is make him sad.

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:56.740
So my only choice is to change this town.

00:09:57.270 --> 00:10:01.580
I'll do anything to bring 
back my darling's smile.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:04.130
I can't just sit around doing nothing!

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:08.370
So for once, we have the same goal.

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:11.470
This'll be a joint venture, 
just between mother and son.

00:10:12.490 --> 00:10:15.800
I hope it'll be the first 
and last time, though.

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:19.780
<i>Mother and son...</i>

00:10:22.770 --> 00:10:25.680
<i>I don't have time to think 
about that right now.</i>

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:28.890
<i>Defeating the enemy in front 
of us is top priority!</i>

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:41.200
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:10:44.390 --> 00:10:45.580
Great Kamaitachi!

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:45.580
Rain of a Thousand Camps!

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:50.700
It dodged!

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:52.500
How is it so fast?

00:10:58.220 --> 00:10:59.270
What's wrong?

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:03.180
Something is bothering me.

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:21.290
There's just one way to save Eve.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:24.740
She needs a transfusion 
of the same blood type.

00:11:25.300 --> 00:11:28.210
But where will you find such rare blood?

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:32.040
This is why I hate useless clods like you.

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:33.040
Victor?

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:35.570
Don't "Victor?" me.

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:39.470
You were planning to ask for my 
help from the start, weren't you?

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:41.970
Well, hurry up and take it.

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:45.510
But I can't take that much blood from you.

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:50.260
Don't worry about me, Vic.

00:11:50.260 --> 00:11:51.110
Eve...

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:53.770
I'll be fine.

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:56.890
Isn't it just about time for your bus?

00:11:57.850 --> 00:12:01.320
If you miss the 9:30 bus, 
you'll miss your exam.

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:04.650
I know you'll pass, Vic.

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:07.800
Go on now. And be safe.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:20.590
Eve!

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:25.360
Of course I'll pass it! I know that!

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:27.140
Don't condescend to me!

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:31.060
Get it done in ten minutes! Even a 
quack like you can manage that, right?

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:35.620
I admire your determination. Well done.

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:40.340
Okay, let's get started.
We don't have a moment to lose!

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:50.000
Thank you, Vic.

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:08.780
I-I can't. Someone take my place.

00:13:08.780 --> 00:13:09.350
Someone—

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:10.890
Alexander Putin!

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:12.060
Pull yourself together!

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:14.980
You're the only one who can save Eve!

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:20.000
Y-You're right.

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:29.040
Eve... Eve...

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:32.100
Please, I'm begging you...

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:34.550
Don't leave me.

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:41.460
Eve...

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:48.500
Wait, Victor!

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:50.970
The parents in front of you now are fakes!

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:52.480
The past can't be changed!

00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:55.270
No matter what you do for them now,
it'll mean nothing!

00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:58.890
<i>My father's tears...</i>

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:01.440
<i>My mother's slender hand.</i>

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:04.150
<i>Even if it's all fake,</i>

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:06.550
<i>how can I stand by and do nothing?</i>

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:20.000
Eve, how do you feel?

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:22.910
Eve...

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:25.750
It's not enough.
Her pulse is still unstable.

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:27.320
She needs more blood!

00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:28.680
Victor, can you handle it?

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:31.800
Of course I can.

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:36.150
Are you sure? You're still so young.

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:38.690
I'm fine! Just shut up!

00:14:39.910 --> 00:14:42.150
See? What did I tell you?

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:44.830
<i>Damn... What can I do?</i>

00:14:52.790 --> 00:14:53.820
I'm sorry.

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:57.250
I guess I'm the one who lost my cool.

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:00.950
There is another AB negative type here.

00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:03.960
It can't be. Such a coincidence...

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:05.770
That doesn't matter now!

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:07.560
Please, believe me!

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:08.760
Hurry and take my blood!

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:10.860
Right.

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:27.940
<i>My blood, the blood of 
a man from the future,</i>

00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:30.860
<i>and my mother, a resident of the past.</i>

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:36.820
<i>Still, it just might be 
possible to change this fate.</i>

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:39.110
Hurry...

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:42.210
Hurry and open your eyes!

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:50.590
Alex...

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:57.620
Th-Thank goodness! Eve!

00:15:57.620 --> 00:16:00.560
<i>I shouldn't be here right now.</i>

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:02.520
Thank goodness!

00:16:00.990 --> 00:16:02.900
<i>This moment belongs to 
the two of them alone.</i>

00:16:05.180 --> 00:16:10.750
<i>Here in this fake world, I just 
saved my possibly fake mother.</i>

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:13.450
<i>I suppose this could be called my atonement.</i>

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:16.750
<i>But this is for the best.</i>

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:20.180
<i>Now, at last... at last...</i>

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:21.110
<i>Something will...</i>

00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:29.030
Victor, your mom will be okay.

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:30.730
Won't you go see her?

00:16:32.150 --> 00:16:34.670
I think you saved her life.

00:16:35.030 --> 00:16:36.620
You ought to commend yourself.

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:39.900
And you deserve a hug from your mom, too.

00:16:43.090 --> 00:16:45.750
I was supposed to be on the bus by now.

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:49.770
I was going to take an 
entrance exam at 10:00,

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:52.780
and once I passed, I'd go to 
university in a bigger city.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.030
And I would never come 
back to this town again!

00:16:59.480 --> 00:17:03.960
I was finally going to get away 
from those stupid parents of mine!

00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:06.480
But because of their idiocy,

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:08.660
now I have to spend another year here.

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:10.960
All they ever do is hold me back!

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:14.300
I've had it! I'd be better off 
if they weren't around—

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:39.310
Victor! Are you all right?

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:43.290
A-Alexander, I—

00:17:44.470 --> 00:17:46.710
How could you do that to my son?

00:17:47.140 --> 00:17:49.880
I'm grateful that you gave 
your blood to my wife,

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:52.640
but I want you to leave now.

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:54.080
Please.

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:57.470
Come on, Victor. Let me look at that.

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:03.010
I would never come back to this town again!

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:07.660
I was finally going to get away 
from those stupid parents of mine!

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:10.710
Stupid? What are you talking about?

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:12.250
It's their fault—

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:13.500
Their fault?

00:19:13.980 --> 00:19:16.630
What have they done besides loving you?

00:19:16.860 --> 00:19:18.920
All they ever do is hold me back!

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:23.600
You don't even realize how blessed 
you are right now. You're the fool!

00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:25.930
Do you know that when 
you're twelve years old,

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:29.020
both of them are going to die?

00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:33.110
Do you understand the meaning 
of the word "irreplaceable"?

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:35.360
I'd be better off if they weren't around!

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:38.150
Why don't you understand?!

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:45.370
Darling!

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:48.250
Don't make that face.
Let's go on our honeymoon.

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:50.790
I'll make you feel better, you poor thing.

00:19:51.090 --> 00:19:54.090
Victor, don't be tied down 
by memories of the past.

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:56.130
All of this is fake.

00:19:56.130 --> 00:20:00.470
What you need to do now is end whatever 
has caused time to turn backwards.

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:03.220
I know that, but...

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:05.760
The two of them are exactly right.

00:20:06.210 --> 00:20:11.690
The Victor my parents wish for is a 
strong, independent winner—a victor.

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:16.460
Not a weakling like you, who can't

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:17.190
Don't Be Misled

00:20:17.170 --> 00:20:18.790
put his parents behind him.

00:20:19.490 --> 00:20:21.610
Mom? I—

00:20:42.240 --> 00:20:44.060
I wanted to atone,

00:20:44.060 --> 00:20:48.010
but I only ended up adding 
more to my pile of sins.

00:20:48.860 --> 00:20:49.760
I'm so tired.

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:53.690
I don't even care about anything anymore.

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:05.280
What the heck is this?

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:19.800
This wall is what's keeping this 
town trapped 34 years in the past.

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:22.630
But who did this? And why?

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:25.850
Hey, hang on! There's a movie 
I want to see next week!

00:21:25.850 --> 00:21:26.710
Blaze...

00:21:27.480 --> 00:21:30.430
Whether or not that'll be 
possible depends on this wall,

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:32.770
and on whoever put it here.

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:38.690
Responsibility and Principle

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:38.730
Responsibility and Principle

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:38.810
Responsibility and Principle

00:21:38.860 --> 00:21:38.900
Responsibility and Principle

00:23:32.550 --> 00:23:40.220
Conjectures and Refutations
